                <pb facs="0358" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg298"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Yours of 29th received. If you are now offered inspection of evidence without
                    restriction upon your communicating the knowledge thus gained and the
                    conclusions thus formed to this Government, accept offer and report with as much
                    particularity as possible, without prejudice, of course, to the right of the
                    United States to inspect the evidence as originally asserted. Hope this
                    inspection, if allowed, as well as opinion of Clunet, will be attended with
                    little delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
